<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scythians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Scythian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scythians were a group of Iranian-speaking nomadic peoples who dominated the Eurasian steppe north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and beyond in the first millennium BCE. Renowned as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mounted-archer">mounted archers</a>, they interacted with and raided the settled empires of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>. They dominated Media for a time according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a> profile, and the Achaemenid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> campaigned against them around 513 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scythians.jpg" alt="Scythians" width="320" height="123" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scythian_Warriors.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
